02:34:12.460 --> 02:34:15.360
So how do they keep the driver and the vital organs of the car cool?

02:34:15.540 --> 02:34:16.320
Well, let me show you.

02:34:16.650 --> 02:34:19.210
Take a look at the left side of the Kenny Schrader Folgers car here.

02:34:19.400 --> 02:34:20.460
They have air vents.

02:34:20.760 --> 02:34:24.790
This upper air vent will carry air through duct tubing down to the rear-end cooler.

02:34:25.140 --> 02:34:29.620
The lower air vent will carry duct air through that piece of tubing down to the oil tank.

02:34:30.000 --> 02:34:34.160
This car has mandated that all oil tanks must be inside the car for a safety precaution.

02:34:34.360 --> 02:34:38.400
The third and possibly most important air vent is on the right side of the car.

02:34:38.730 --> 02:34:43.980
This is the air vent here, this baby right here, that carries air through and dumps it on the driver.

02:34:44.200 --> 02:34:45.120
Why is it so important?

02:34:45.180 --> 02:34:49.210
Because this side window in a car prevents any air from getting inside of the driver.

02:34:49.470 --> 02:34:55.000
And you literally could cook a Winston Cup driver here at 145 degrees on a hot July afternoon.

