There are less than two laps to go in the Pepsi 400.

03:06:59.060 --> 03:07:00.000
And Morgan stays about.

03:07:02.550 --> 03:07:22.730
Then does Davey Allison. His car is really working. Let's watch him when he goes into turn three. Davey opens up a little distance on the straightaway, but when you go into the turn, Davey's going to go a little bit high. Well, this time he keeps it down lower than he's been. He perhaps looks in his rearview mirror and saw where Morgan Shepard is making it up that time. Morgan moves right back up on him. Has to come around now to get the white flag.

03:07:23.150 --> 03:07:29.980
Carol Kinder has the white flag in hand, and he waves it for Davey Allison and Morgan Shepard.

03:07:31.530 --> 03:07:39.900
Parsons, they're on the last tour of the 2.500. It is Allison that is staying out front by

03:07:39.900 --> 03:07:59.980
about a car length over Morgan Shepard as Bill at just a little in third position. They come out of the 31 degrees of banking and down the flat backstretch for the final time and they pass by Darrell Walter who is successful here at this racetrack in February in the Daytona 500. Now the cars set themselves into turn number one.

03:08:02.170 --> 03:08:10.700
That's Morgan's wife, Sandra, Sandra, is just hoping and praying everything she has that Morgan can pull out the victory.

03:08:10.920 --> 03:08:13.040
Let's see, we have a battle for third position.

03:08:13.220 --> 03:08:15.580
The win is going to be by Davey Allison.

03:08:15.920 --> 03:08:17.620
He crosses the drive and wins.

03:08:17.980 --> 03:08:23.120
Morgan is second, and Bill Parsons, I believe, got third at the last moment, passing Bill Elliott.

03:08:24.530 --> 03:08:27.750
There's Davey Allison, a happy fellow inside that car.

03:08:27.810 --> 03:08:29.250
